<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  A Dog Said... Animal Prosthetics 2 (Workshop 3238353862, packageId SamBucher.ADogSaidAnimalProsthetics2).

  That mod sorts animals into three categories by listing them in the recipeUsers of three abstract
  recipes, ADS_Cat1 (peg legs and the like), ADS_Cat2 (simple prosthetic limbs) and ADS_Cat3 (full
  bionics). A category includes the ones below it, so an animal of category 3 is listed in all three.
  Its own patch then copies those lists into the surgery recipes, which is why this mod loads BEFORE it
  (About.xml, loadBefore): a name added after that copy is never offered any surgery.

  Only applied when that mod is active; nothing here changes the game otherwise. PatchOperationFindMod
  matches by mod name.

  The beetle is a trainable pack animal: category 3.

  The seraph is deliberately left out. Those surgeries name the vanilla body part defs, and every part
  of the seraph is its own (ACS_AngelArms, ACS_AngelLegs...), so no surgery of that mod could apply to
  it: listing it would add a name that is never offered anything. The beetle is in the same position
  for its legs, claws, horn and elytra (ACS_BeetleLeg, ACS_BeetleClaw...); only its vanilla parts (Eye,
  Antenna) can be concerned, and which of them the other mod has a surgery for is not verified here.
  Adding the mod's own parts to those surgeries would mean patching the
  other mod's recipes one by one, and is not done.
-->
<Patch>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>A Dog Said... Animal Prosthetics 2</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[@Name="ADS_Cat1" or @Name="ADS_Cat2" or @Name="ADS_Cat3"]/recipeUsers</xpath>
      <value>
        <li>ACS_DarkMatterBeetle</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
